WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.753 --> 00:00:05.171
In Texas,

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:08.800
the monarch is close to exhaustion.

00:00:10.301 --> 00:00:12.554
With her last reserves,

00:00:12.554 --> 00:00:15.306
she's seeking out the perfect spot
to lay her eggs.

00:00:18.768 --> 00:00:21.813
Using her amazing sense of smell

00:00:21.813 --> 00:00:23.982
she's on the hunt for milkweed,

00:00:23.982 --> 00:00:26.443
the only food her babies will eat.

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:30.780
It's a plant

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:35.410
which was once abundant.

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:41.875
But now over three quarters of the state
is farmland,

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:45.128
choked by pesticides and weed killers.

00:00:46.796 --> 00:00:50.884
For a butterfly, it's effectively
a desert.

00:00:56.264 --> 00:00:57.515
It's not just farms

00:00:57.515 --> 00:01:01.644
that have replaced wild landscapes.

00:01:03.646 --> 00:01:06.357
Reaching the suburbs of Austin,

00:01:06.357 --> 00:01:08.485
she's running on empty.

00:01:10.361 --> 00:01:12.238
But incredibly

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:15.742
in flight from over 400 feet away

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:18.620
she's found the needle in the haystack.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.085
This backyard

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:28.880
has exactly what she needs for her eggs.

00:01:36.513 --> 00:01:39.182
She lays hundreds on milkweed

00:01:39.182 --> 00:01:44.562
specially planted
to help migrating monarchs.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.611
But she'll never meet her babies.

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:59.119
Before they even hatch

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:04.624
she takes her last breath.

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:06.209
Her mission

00:02:06.209 --> 00:02:08.503
is complete.

00:02:11.506 --> 00:02:12.924
This is the true

00:02:12.924 --> 00:02:17.220
miracle of the monarch migration.

00:02:18.388 --> 00:02:22.517
It's not a marathon.

00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:25.311
It's a relay race.

00:02:30.608 --> 00:02:35.655
After about four days,

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:39.826
her caterpillars
hatch in the perfect nursery,

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:43.580
surrounded by food.

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:48.126
And that's all this little bug has on her
mind.

00:02:49.961 --> 00:02:54.007
Milkweed is poisonous,

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:57.093
yet she's not only immune.

00:02:57.093 --> 00:02:59.596
She's using it for her own defense,

00:03:00.638 --> 00:03:02.891
storing the deadly chemicals in her body.

00:03:04.058 --> 00:03:12.192
She makes herself
toxic, wearing bright colors

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:15.695
as a warning signal.

00:03:19.991 --> 00:03:21.868
In just two weeks,

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:24.913
she'll eat and grow.

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:27.248
And eat.

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:28.958
And grow.

00:03:31.669 --> 00:03:32.545
Until she's

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:36.716
3000 times bigger.

00:03:37.759 --> 00:03:43.223
Spinning sticky silk to hang from.

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:48.519
She forms a chrysalis.

00:03:58.238 --> 00:04:00.156
Over the next ten days,

00:04:00.156 --> 00:04:03.409
she breaks herself down
into a kind of genetic soup.

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:10.917
Before putting herself back together,

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.885
and emerging

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:25.306
as a butterfly.

00:04:30.853 --> 00:04:33.731
She's her mother's daughter, born

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:38.278
born with the same mission

00:04:43.241 --> 00:04:45.285
and the same built in G.P.S.

